<section class="shell band">
  <h1>LPC supervision in Texas</h1>
  {#- Most of this page's traffic arrives from the licensure guide rather than
      from /for-therapists/, so it never meets the argument the hub makes. One
      line of it before the specification. -#}
  <p class="intro-wide">Most associates pick a supervisor on price and proximity, because that
  is what the listings show. You will spend eighteen months to three years with this one, and
  it is the stretch that sets how you practice afterwards. Interview more than one before you
  sign, and the <a href="/texas-lpc-licensure/">Texas licensure guide</a> lists the questions
  worth asking, whoever you end up choosing.</p>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Reem Glasco has been a Texas Licensed Professional Counselor Supervisor since
    {{ site.supervisorSince }}.
    Supervision is online and available anywhere in Texas, and includes three individual
    hours and one group hour each month. Places are capped deliberately, so ask about
    current availability. Equine-assisted sessions near
    Dripping Springs are optional, and EMDR consultation is free while you are an
    associate here.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="intro-wide">Places are filled by application rather than inquiry: a CV, three
  professional references and written answers to seven questions, with verification before an
  agreement is signed.</p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="cta" href="/contact/appointment/">Request a consult</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--night">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>The arrangement, in numbers</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>Monthly fee</dt><dd>$425</dd></div>
      <div><dt>What that includes</dt><dd>Three individual supervision hours and one group hour each month, four hours in total</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Caseload assumption</dt><dd>Ten or more clients a week</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Format</dt><dd>Online only, statewide in Texas</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Openings</dt><dd>Capped; ask about current availability</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Agency contracts</dt><dd>Three-month contracts for associates inside an agency or group practice, $500 a month</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Placement site</dt><dd>Online only</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Equine sessions</dt><dd>Optional, $60 each, Dripping Springs, Texas</dd></div>
      <div><dt>EMDR consultation</dt><dd>Free individual consults while you are supervised here</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Retreats</dt><dd>Annual mindful trail retreat for associates and therapists</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Consult</dt><dd>Free, thirty minutes, Zoom or phone</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>Why three individual plus one group: Texas asks for at least four supervision hours a
      month, and no more than half of them may be group. Three and one is exactly four, with
      group at a quarter of the total.</p>
    <p>That meets the floor rather than clearing it, so a missed session is made up inside the
      same month rather than absorbed.
      <a href="/texas-lpc-licensure/">The rules are laid out in full in the licensure
      guide</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--sand">
  <div class="shell">
  <h2>What Texas requires of you</h2>
  <p>The Texas requirements are specific, and the part that trips people up is not the total
  hours. It is the floor on months, the split between direct and indirect, and the group
  supervision cap.</p>
  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>3,000 hours</dt><dd>Supervised experience required for full LPC licensure</dd></div>
    <div><dt>1,500 of them</dt><dd>Must be direct client counseling contact</dd></div>
    <div><dt>18 months</dt><dd>The minimum, no matter how fast you accrue hours</dd></div>
    <div><dt>4 hours a month</dt><dd>Minimum supervision, with no more than half in a group</dd></div>
    <div><dt>60 months</dt><dd>When your LPC Associate license expires, without renewal</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="cta" href="/texas-lpc-licensure/">Read the full guide</a>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

